// BUG-920: the Ring channel-safety warning asked `k == TYPE_POINTER ||
// k == TYPE_OPAQUE` — the hand-rolled carrier disjunction the
// audit_carrier_dispatch gate exists to freeze. Of the four shapes that put a
// pointer through a channel, only the BARE one warned.
//
// One file per shape ON PURPOSE: all four emit the same text, so a single file
// with four pushes would pass warn_check even if three regressed.
//
// ADVISORY, and the ledger says so precisely: the SAFETY half (pushing a pointer
// to a LOCAL) is carrier-complete already via container_push_arg_escapes, which
// rejects all four. This warning is about a pointer the RECEIVER may not be able
// to use.
Ring(*u32, 4) c;
u32 gx;
u32 main() { c.push(&gx); return 0; }
